{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310822-amkhata-and-deceived","id":310822,"title":"Amkhata and Deceived","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-12T20:18:56-08:00","id":310822,"title":"Amkhata and Deceived","content":"It seems like the Deceived have quite a complicated relationship with Amkhata. If the Temakh are to be believed, such creatures started as offspring of the Devourer (something I don't think was made explicitly clear in the Mummy core book). A battle with a particularly nasty Amkhat was responsible for the corruption of each of the Shan'iatu. The Temakh have universally negative views of Ammut, even if they cannot bring themselves to blame her for their current predicament. And it seems Fate does not like the idea of Seba being consumed, putting it at odds with the tendency for Amkhata to devour such relics if they ever get the chance. That's a lot stacked against the use of Amkhata to begin with, even if they aren't necessarily bound by the same edicts on blasphemy as Arisen.<br /> <br /> That said, we know from Cursed Necropolis D.C. that some Deceived most certainly do make use of Amkhata, even to the extent of mixing Seba into the creation process. The Rotting Temple write-up mentions temples containing tapestries capable of calling Amkhata. It's not a lot, but a few Deceived clearly have some kind of positive relationship with chimeras.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that the two near-identical, Keeper-aligned, nature-obsessed Movements, the Rotting Temple and Scions of the Emerald Ankh, stand on opposite sides of this debate as a by-product of their respective nature-as-corruption and nature-as-purity philosophies. The Emerald Ankh explicitly opposes the creation of Lifeless, whereas the Rotting Temple would see Lesser Amkhata produced by the destruction of relics as, perhaps, the very embodiment of their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Outside of these two extremes, however, there isn't a whole lot on the attitudes of Deceived in general towards Amkhata. At the moment I'm inclined to just treat them as dangerous animals if a rogue one were to be encountered, and as tools (dangerous in the hands of the enemy, useful in the hands of a friend) if they are clearly being driven by a master. I'm not entirely sure though. Without the ability to create Sadikh, a Greater Amkhata seems like it would be a pretty useful supernatural heavyweight to have on side, and a useful guardian to watch over your tomb.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:33:37-08:00","id":310932,"title":"","content":"I'm more interested in the relationship between Amkhata and Shuankhsen, myself. I could see Bane Affinities for dealing with those little beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:43:51-08:00","id":311113,"title":"","content":"I kind of liked better imagining that amkhata are from some nether-realm unrelated to Ammut or Duat.<br /> <br /> I also liked imagining the Shan'iatu were aliens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:48:55-08:00","id":311119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310822-amkhata-and-deceived?p=310932#post310932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested in the relationship between Amkhata and Shuankhsen, myself. I could see Bane Affinities for dealing with those little beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the only existing Bane Relic in the game is for taming Amkhata, I think it's safe to say that Shuankhsen and Amkhata have a pretty close-knit relationship. The fact that BotD indicates they share a connection to Ammut just reinforces that. There's not a whole lot of ambiguity around it.<br /> <br /> Deceived, on the other hand, don't seem to have the &quot;standard&quot; response to Amkhata that Shuankhsen and Arisen have to fall back on. Speaking in generalities, any Shuankhsen that can get an Amkhata to serve it is probably happy for it to do so, while any Arisen would prefer to destroy the vile blasphemy before it. How Deceived react is... a great deal more up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T07:50:45-08:00","id":311275,"title":"","content":"Well I guess Deceived woul view Amkhata as useful but dangerous tools. They wouldn't be so afraid of using them like the Arisen because they can't be tainted by Ammut like them do I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}